      },
      "text_excerpt": "# Analyte Reference Ranges, Laboratory Handbook",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182216+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0002",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 2,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 49,
        "char_end": 308
      },
      "text_excerpt": "Reference intervals used when reviewing returned result sheets. Source: the published\nreference ranges for blood tests compiled at\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reference_ranges_for_blood_tests (publi",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182244+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0003",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 3,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 310,
        "char_end": 550
      },
      "text_excerpt": "A reference interval is the range within which the central 95 percent of a healthy reference\npopulation falls. It is a review aid, not a diagnosis: a value outside the interval is a\nresult to look at,",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182259+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0004",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 4,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 552,
        "char_end": 555
      },
      "text_excerpt": "---",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182266+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0005",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 5,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 557,
        "char_end": 601
      },
      "text_excerpt": "## Section One , Reference intervals by test",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182273+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0006",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 6,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 603,
        "char_end": 721
      },
      "text_excerpt": "Note that the interval and its unit are recorded in separate columns, which is how the\npublished source presents them.",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182289+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0007",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 7,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 723,
        "char_end": 965
      },
      "text_excerpt": "| Test | Reference range | Unit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sodium | 135–145 | mmol/L |\n| Potassium | 3.5–5.0 | mmol/L |\n| Chloride | 95–105 | mmol/L |\n| Total calcium | 2.1–2.5 | mmol/L |\n| Albumin | 35–55 | g/L |\n| Total bilirubin | 1.7–17 | umol/L |",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182322+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0008",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 8,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 967,
        "char_end": 1002
      },
      "text_excerpt": "## Section Two , Panel completeness",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182329+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0009",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 9,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 1004,
        "char_end": 1219
      },
      "text_excerpt": "A returned result sheet states, for every result: the sample identifier, the test, the\nmeasured value and the analysing laboratory. A result missing any of these cannot be\nreconciled against the sheet",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182340+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0010",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 10,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 1221,
        "char_end": 1256
      },
      "text_excerpt": "## Section Three , Sheet arithmetic",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182347+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0011",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 11,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 1258,
        "char_end": 1484
      },
      "text_excerpt": "Where a sheet declares a batch, the sum of the declared result counts for each laboratory\nequals the declared total result count for the sheet. A total that does not follow from its\nparts cannot be re",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182357+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0012",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 12,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 1486,
        "char_end": 1528
      },
      "text_excerpt": "## Section Four , Consistency requirements",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182364+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0013",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 13,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 1530,
        "char_end": 1601
      },
      "text_excerpt": "A result sheet is internally consistent when all of the following hold:",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182371+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0014",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 14,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 1603,
        "char_end": 1875
      },
      "text_excerpt": "1. Every measured value falls inside the reference range recorded for its test in Section One.\n2. Every result states its sample identifier, its test, its measured value and its\n   analysing laborator",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182385+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0015",
      "input_type": "context",
      "document_id": "analyte_reference_ranges",
      "document_name": "analyte_reference_ranges.md",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "paragraph": 15,
        "sentence": 1,
        "char_start": 1877,
        "char_end": 2076
      },
      "text_excerpt": "A value outside its reference interval is recorded with the figure and the interval it falls\noutside. The assessment records what is inconsistent and leaves interpretation to the\nreporting clinician.",
      "cited_by": [],
      "first_indexed": "2026-09-17T22:37:44.182395+00:00"
    },
    {
      "ref_id": "REF-0016",
